WEBVTT

00:01.192 --> 00:04.029
(La La La La Girls)

00:04.029 --> 00:07.366
(Vocaloid Song Charades)

00:07.949 --> 00:09.534
(La La La La Girls)

00:09.534 --> 00:10.952
- La La...
- La La...

00:10.952 --> 00:12.412
Girls here!

00:12.412 --> 00:14.122
- Today...
- Today?

00:14.122 --> 00:16.249
It's another fan favorite!

00:16.249 --> 00:17.457
What is it?

00:17.457 --> 00:20.503
Virtual Singer Song Charades!

00:21.379 --> 00:24.924
Let's do "Lion Dance"
for our next cover!

00:24.924 --> 00:27.135
I'm telling you!

00:27.135 --> 00:30.638
We have to do "Robo's House"
before "Lion Dance."

00:30.638 --> 00:32.265
You agree, don't you?

00:32.265 --> 00:34.559
I guess...

00:36.185 --> 00:40.064
Erea-chan, you said
it was okay the other day...

00:40.064 --> 00:42.692
But today's a new day.

00:43.359 --> 00:48.072
Sanpo P's songs are...
not so great, huh?

00:49.741 --> 00:52.869
I would like your opinion
on how I sing this part.

00:53.536 --> 00:56.289
Personally, I'd say it's terrible.

00:56.289 --> 00:59.959
Come on! This part definitely
needs to be growled out!

00:59.959 --> 01:03.379
Why is it so hard to understand?
Re-record it!

01:07.550 --> 01:10.006
(Can't believe it was leaked, haha)
See how the video from the other day is blowing up?

01:10.006 --> 01:11.804
(I bet the staff can't stand her either)
See how the video from the other day is blowing up?

01:11.804 --> 01:13.431
That was too easy.

01:13.431 --> 01:18.186
We should still come up with new moves.
Numbers are important.

01:34.118 --> 01:35.453
It's over.

01:41.501 --> 01:42.794
It's in the past!

01:42.794 --> 01:44.671
Loose lips sink ships!

01:44.671 --> 01:48.341
I'll push through today
without talking or singing!

01:48.341 --> 01:50.259
Let's go!

02:00.061 --> 02:04.649
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype

02:05.566 --> 02:10.279
The story always revolves around us

02:10.279 --> 02:15.368
That may be a given, but let me repeat it

02:15.368 --> 02:20.413
Can you read the guidelines?
No matter how carefully we write them

02:20.623 --> 02:25.544
Why does something always get in the way?
Still, we'll make it roar!

02:25.544 --> 02:29.548
In a heartbeat, like an overdrive

02:29.548 --> 02:36.347
We yearn to distort the world we see

02:36.347 --> 02:41.185
Seeing too clearly makes innocence
seem ridiculous, what a joke!

02:41.185 --> 02:46.107
Even vain attempts at being brave
Will be rewarded when the time comes

02:46.107 --> 02:49.944
This is the plot of our survival

02:49.944 --> 02:55.700
Rewriting the tale
Shedding absurd tears, the newtype way

02:55.700 --> 03:00.371
We can go anywhere, we can, so don't stop now

03:00.371 --> 03:04.959
Not an anime, not real either,
let's make our own category

03:04.959 --> 03:08.129
We've grown tired
of this complicated, dull world!

03:08.129 --> 03:11.465
Leave it to us, we'll write our own dreams

03:11.674 --> 03:15.011
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype, our choice

03:15.011 --> 03:16.637
Following the steady beat

03:16.637 --> 03:21.559
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype

03:23.603 --> 03:27.231
Back in middle school,
I used to be in a group.

03:28.542 --> 03:33.631
We'd post videos
of our covers and chats together.

03:34.380 --> 03:35.881
It was fun.

03:37.599 --> 03:42.270
But then, a strange video was uploaded,
and our activities ended.

03:43.247 --> 03:45.625
(How to deal with online slander?)

03:47.502 --> 03:49.128
I was terrified.

03:49.875 --> 03:53.699
I couldn't even go outside
or talk anymore.

03:56.928 --> 04:00.515
But I don't want it to end like this.

04:00.910 --> 04:03.204
I want to have dreams again.

04:04.018 --> 04:04.809
(Magical Physical Kululu)

04:04.809 --> 04:10.149
(Magical Physical Kululu)
I want to sing, talk, and share what I love.

04:10.858 --> 04:13.277
I want to tell everyone!

04:14.529 --> 04:17.323
Nakamachi-san, just observing today?

04:17.323 --> 04:20.576
But I just can't be in a group!

04:42.932 --> 04:49.647
(Playing the guitar!
(Nonoka)

04:52.525 --> 04:54.485
Yay!

04:55.111 --> 04:58.363
"Nono-chan,
you play the guitar so well."

04:58.363 --> 04:59.699
Thanks!

04:59.699 --> 05:04.036
"Congratulations on forming MewType."
Thank you!

05:04.036 --> 05:09.916
"It's Yuno-chi's song."
Good ear! The last song was hers!

05:09.916 --> 05:12.086
"The MewType artwork is so cute!"

05:12.086 --> 05:16.299
Right? Miyako-chan drew it for us!

05:16.299 --> 05:20.011
"It's Yako Fujimi-sensei." Oh?

05:20.011 --> 05:24.807
"With a weekly series and a band,
I'm worried Yako-sensei might collapse."

05:25.558 --> 05:28.154
It's okay, I'll give her first aid!

05:28.811 --> 05:30.688
"Her drawings were rough"?

05:31.898 --> 05:35.693
Abracadabra... It's fixed!

05:35.693 --> 05:38.529
Nono-chan, the bath's ready!

05:38.529 --> 05:42.074
Ugh! Nana's coming! It's bath time!

05:42.074 --> 05:46.829
Thanks for coming again today.
See you next time!

05:46.829 --> 05:49.707
Whoa!

05:53.210 --> 05:56.464
I'll end the lesson here.
You can write this down.

06:06.682 --> 06:07.434
Fuji-san.

06:07.434 --> 06:08.435
Here!

06:08.435 --> 06:13.314
I know your manga is important,
but you should take notes for the test.

06:13.314 --> 06:15.107
Yes, I'm sorry.

06:15.107 --> 06:18.515
Hey, you! Live streaming in class
is against the rules.

06:18.515 --> 06:20.517
Come to the teacher's office later.

06:22.156 --> 06:25.034
Thank you for your submission,
Fujimi-sensei.

06:25.034 --> 06:27.495
Last week's reader polls

06:27.495 --> 06:31.975
were also very promising
for a newcomer's first series.

06:31.975 --> 06:33.291
I'm glad.

06:33.291 --> 06:37.380
Must be tough handling
the series, school, and the band.

06:37.380 --> 06:41.300
When the deadline is close,
they let me skip practice.

06:41.300 --> 06:42.635
Thank goodness!

06:42.635 --> 06:46.430
I was going to ask to make it biweekly
if it was too much for you,

06:46.430 --> 06:50.451
but I'd like to keep this momentum,
so let's do our best!

06:50.451 --> 06:52.061
Okay.

06:52.061 --> 06:54.689
(The meeting has ended)

07:05.449 --> 07:07.326
Before practice starts,

07:07.326 --> 07:11.038
I have good and bad news,
so pick one for me.

07:11.038 --> 07:12.832
Good news!

07:12.832 --> 07:13.838
Okay.

07:17.962 --> 07:20.631
We have a new avatar!

07:20.631 --> 07:21.882
Maru-kun!

07:21.882 --> 07:26.137
I noticed you had it in the corner
of everyone's character design.

07:26.721 --> 07:28.431
Thank you very much.

07:28.431 --> 07:32.351
And thank you for always
meeting the deadlines.

07:33.019 --> 07:35.521
And now, here's the bad news.

07:37.565 --> 07:40.526
MewType's social media account
is getting flamed.

07:45.262 --> 07:46.782
She logged out.

07:46.782 --> 07:48.409
Nakamachi-san!

07:48.659 --> 07:49.702
I haven't even said anything.

07:49.702 --> 07:51.078
- Miyanaga-san is the one getting slammed.
- I haven't even said anything.

07:51.078 --> 07:51.708
- Miyanaga-san is the one getting slammed.
- Loose lips are trouble. Keep quiet, keep quiet.

07:51.708 --> 07:52.733
- What?
- Loose lips are trouble. Keep quiet, keep quiet.

07:52.733 --> 07:55.416
- There's no smoke without fire.
- Loose lips are trouble. Keep quiet, keep quiet.

07:55.416 --> 07:57.626
- This is just arson-level slander!
- I won't talk, so don't hate on me.

07:57.626 --> 08:01.172
It all started with a comment
from Fuji-san's fan.

08:01.172 --> 08:04.300
They were worried you might be too busy,

08:04.300 --> 08:08.345
and Miyanaga-san said
it was okay if she collapsed.

08:08.345 --> 08:09.930
I did?

08:09.930 --> 08:13.184
"It's okay, I'll give her first aid!"

08:13.184 --> 08:15.770
It sounds like she's just worried.

08:15.770 --> 08:17.480
(She isn't actually worried) Yes, but they thought
she was assuming she'd collapse

08:17.480 --> 08:19.982
(It's all pretty talk) Yes, but they thought
she was assuming she'd collapse

08:19.982 --> 08:20.608
(It's all pretty talk)
and took it the wrong way.

08:20.608 --> 08:21.859
(Hypocrite)
and took it the wrong way.

08:21.859 --> 08:23.486
I see.

08:29.992 --> 08:31.160
Are you okay?

08:31.160 --> 08:34.747
Yeah! Nono-chan's kingdom is at peace.

08:34.747 --> 08:35.873
Okay, then.

08:39.752 --> 08:41.003
Miyako-chan.

08:41.754 --> 08:44.090
Don't overthink it.

08:44.965 --> 08:45.966
Okay?

08:45.966 --> 08:50.804
I'll set guidelines, but I can't
prevent mean live comments.

08:50.804 --> 08:55.142
I think it's best to put
live streaming on hold for now.

08:56.710 --> 08:59.296
Now, let's start practice!

08:59.296 --> 09:01.440
Okay.

09:02.232 --> 09:03.568
Welcome to...

09:03.568 --> 09:06.712
Maru-kun's Counseling Time!

09:06.712 --> 09:08.823
Squish squish!

09:08.823 --> 09:10.699
So, what's bothering you?

09:13.202 --> 09:18.958
I, a depressing loser,
caused trouble for a bright chad.

09:18.958 --> 09:22.253
Huh? What do you mean by "Abracadabra"?

09:22.253 --> 09:25.506
It's so obvious
you don't care about nerds.

09:25.506 --> 09:30.344
I'm sensitive to things like that.
You shiny chads wouldn't get it.

09:30.344 --> 09:32.346
You're losing it.

09:34.557 --> 09:38.519
I should've read the contract carefully.

09:38.519 --> 09:43.149
Oh, the band? You were totally
blinded by your drawing work.

09:43.149 --> 09:45.901
I'm pushing myself to the limit

09:45.901 --> 09:49.738
with manga, drawing, and the band
to gain more skills.

09:49.738 --> 09:54.368
I'm not talented enough
to live off manga alone.

09:54.368 --> 09:56.203
I know that.

09:57.270 --> 09:59.999
Well, it's better to have more skills.

09:59.999 --> 10:01.208
That's right!

10:01.208 --> 10:05.965
In order to survive this chaotic world,
I'll do whatever I can!

10:05.965 --> 10:07.756
I'm lucky just to have...

10:08.424 --> 10:09.884
Are you having a seizure?

10:18.392 --> 10:21.227
I need comfort! I need more comfort!

10:28.027 --> 10:36.577
You're such a cutie...
Only cuteness can comfort me...

10:52.134 --> 10:55.511
"You have a deadline!
You have a deadline!"

10:55.511 --> 10:56.764
(2 AM: Storyboards 15 & 16
8 AM: 5 chibi character sketches)

10:56.764 --> 10:57.973
(2 AM: Storyboards 15 & 16
8 AM: 5 chibi character sketches) All right!

10:58.891 --> 11:03.102
I'll send the storyboard by midnight
and five chibi sketches by dawn!

11:03.102 --> 11:06.023
I'll survive this!

11:08.525 --> 11:10.937
Uh... Are you all right?

11:10.937 --> 11:13.489
You've got bags under your eyes.

11:13.489 --> 11:16.158
Haven't you slept?
You should probably...

11:16.158 --> 11:17.451
I'm fine.

11:17.952 --> 11:22.164
I'm totally okay... I can play...

11:22.164 --> 11:25.793
I'll keep... going...

11:30.714 --> 11:33.092
Huh? She fell asleep?

11:33.092 --> 11:36.095
I'll contact her family.

11:43.285 --> 11:45.120
I have to give her first aid!

11:54.989 --> 11:56.865
I fell asleep.

11:57.616 --> 12:02.121
I need to get the lines fixed
and brief the assistants by noon.

12:02.121 --> 12:05.708
I'll practice the keyboard
on my lunch break.

12:05.708 --> 12:06.875
The revised artwork
should arrive by noon,

12:06.875 --> 12:08.794
- The revised artwork should arrive by noon,
- Good morning, Miyako-chan.

12:08.794 --> 12:11.755
so I'll handle it immediately if needed.

12:15.634 --> 12:17.845
Good morning.

12:17.845 --> 12:21.544
You're already at school?
Are you studying early today?

12:24.350 --> 12:28.794
I'm sorry for causing trouble
with our social media account...

12:28.794 --> 12:29.940
Huh?!

12:29.940 --> 12:32.609
- What are you...
- Halfsies.

12:32.609 --> 12:33.788
Huh?

12:35.777 --> 12:38.365
We hugged. Now, we're even.

12:42.870 --> 12:45.248
Huh?

12:45.248 --> 12:46.583
I can't do this.

13:01.063 --> 13:03.932
This week's Chupa-Satu is so good!

13:03.932 --> 13:08.479
There's something magical
about Yako Fujimi-sensei's works.

13:08.479 --> 13:12.857
No matter how awful things get,
she's the only one who can soothe me.

13:19.131 --> 13:22.701
I wish I could
do something for her too...

13:22.701 --> 13:27.373
Oh, there you are! Arale-chan!

13:27.998 --> 13:31.627
Let's eat lunch together.

13:36.702 --> 13:38.747
You're really here.

13:38.747 --> 13:39.936
Yep!

13:39.936 --> 13:40.969
Miyanaga-san!

13:40.969 --> 13:43.472
We go to the same school?!

13:43.472 --> 13:45.224
That's right.

13:48.261 --> 13:51.449
Miyako-chan and I
are both 2nd-year students,

13:51.449 --> 13:54.357
but that was the first time we met.

13:54.357 --> 13:58.570
I'm in Class A, and she's in Class B.

13:59.154 --> 14:02.658
Class B is right above mine!

14:02.658 --> 14:06.620
Knowing that Yako-sensei
is working so hard right above me

14:06.620 --> 14:09.623
makes me want to do
my best at school too!

14:14.712 --> 14:15.921
Arale-chan?

14:32.771 --> 14:36.900
Do you understand how I feel about you?

14:42.156 --> 14:43.157
No.

14:43.657 --> 14:49.037
The bang, the squeeze, the pounding...
Don't you feel it?

14:49.037 --> 14:50.164
Not at all.

14:50.164 --> 14:54.460
Then, my hug this morning
didn't get through either.

14:55.294 --> 14:57.838
We really have to talk it out.

14:59.651 --> 15:00.846
She knows...

15:02.384 --> 15:05.512
But... if I talk...

15:08.724 --> 15:12.644
Have you known Miyako-chan for a while?

15:13.145 --> 15:16.858
Of course! Yako-sensei
is an incredible manga artist!

15:16.858 --> 15:18.692
First, I fell for her art!

15:18.692 --> 15:22.529
Then, I spent hours browsing drawing websites
with my phone when I was in 6th grade!

15:22.529 --> 15:27.034
I read all her works!
And her characters are so...

15:30.454 --> 15:34.833
You really like Miyako-chan a lot,
don't you?

15:34.833 --> 15:37.002
That's so embarrassing!

15:39.118 --> 15:40.255
Arale-chan.

15:41.570 --> 15:44.823
You should tell her that you like her!

15:45.664 --> 15:50.541
She hasn't been doing great.
I think that could cheer her up.

15:51.725 --> 15:54.478
There's power in love.

15:55.309 --> 15:56.980
"Power"?

15:56.980 --> 15:59.858
Let's give Miyako-chan a smooch!

16:02.778 --> 16:06.156
A smooch?!

16:06.740 --> 16:10.577
I have to fix the artwork,
finish up the manuscript...

16:10.577 --> 16:12.521
Then, I have
to practice the keyboard...

16:18.627 --> 16:20.546
- Is that candy?
- Miyako-chan!

16:21.797 --> 16:23.757
You know the three-second rule?

16:24.341 --> 16:26.802
Ready? Go!

16:26.802 --> 16:29.221
One, two, three seconds.

16:29.221 --> 16:31.765
One, two, three seconds.

16:32.266 --> 16:33.934
Why am I doing this?

16:35.621 --> 16:39.898
I'll go get Miyako-chan,
so wait right here.

16:39.898 --> 16:42.818
Let's lure her with candy!

16:42.818 --> 16:45.070
Let's go!

16:45.070 --> 16:49.533
But more importantly...
I have to show my love with a smooch?

16:49.533 --> 16:52.286
One, two, three, here.

16:52.286 --> 16:55.122
One, two, three, here.

16:55.122 --> 16:57.958
One, two, three, here.

16:57.958 --> 17:01.128
One, two, three, here.

17:01.128 --> 17:04.298
One, two, three, here.

17:04.298 --> 17:07.301
One, two, three, here.

17:07.301 --> 17:12.180
Look, Miyako-chan!
Here is the candy house!

17:12.180 --> 17:13.682
Over here!

17:15.183 --> 17:16.727
Ya... Yako-sensei!

17:16.727 --> 17:18.186
Nakamachi-san?

17:18.186 --> 17:21.690
I apologize for calling you out
on such a fine day.

17:22.941 --> 17:24.651
It's the manager.

17:24.651 --> 17:25.361
What?!

17:25.361 --> 17:29.196
It's the sticker that I lined up all day for
but got sold out right in front of my eyes!

17:29.196 --> 17:32.326
It's the super rare
limited edition sticker!

17:33.076 --> 17:38.205
It became even harder to get
with the anti-scalper measures!

17:38.205 --> 17:41.667
It's the Toyoshima Super Highland
limited sticker!

17:47.132 --> 17:49.176
You can do it, Arale-chan!

17:49.926 --> 17:52.471
- Yako Fujimi-sensei!
- Yes!

17:52.471 --> 17:55.057
I first came across your work

17:55.057 --> 17:59.061
when my friend's sister showed me
a Magilulu illustration.

17:59.061 --> 18:01.063
It stole my heart right away.

18:01.063 --> 18:05.484
After that, I spent hours browsing
drawing websites on my birthday gift phone.

18:05.484 --> 18:09.488
Your Magilulu fan art
had the most likes

18:09.488 --> 18:12.115
and details like no one else's.

18:12.115 --> 18:17.204
In every single stroke, I could feel
your love for the characters.

18:17.204 --> 18:20.165
I was amazed at how you expressed
so much through art.

18:20.165 --> 18:23.085
Before I knew it,
I was following all your updates.

18:23.085 --> 18:27.172
Oh, and your manga series too!
I absolutely love...

18:32.184 --> 18:34.645
Oh no...

18:38.642 --> 18:39.893
Arale-chan?

18:44.356 --> 18:46.650
She definitely thinks I'm weird.

18:47.359 --> 18:50.654
I knew I shouldn't have said anything!

18:53.198 --> 18:54.700
Oh, I'm sorry!

18:58.205 --> 19:00.955
I wasn't supposed to use this station!

19:16.462 --> 19:20.674
To think I changed stations
after running into her last time...

19:22.998 --> 19:26.626
The more I try to avoid her...

19:28.523 --> 19:30.992
Back then, I should've...

19:59.306 --> 20:02.309
(Magical Physical Kululu)

20:02.696 --> 20:05.199
I absolutely love...

20:11.018 --> 20:13.311
I should have another one somewhere...

20:15.761 --> 20:19.640
"Dreams are power!"

20:33.724 --> 20:35.934
Arale-chan, good morning!

20:37.302 --> 20:38.804
You can't talk?

20:39.805 --> 20:41.640
I see.

20:44.309 --> 20:46.936
Miyako-chan, good morning!

20:49.564 --> 20:52.067
Thank you for yesterday.

20:54.402 --> 20:55.654
Here you go!

20:56.279 --> 20:57.906
It didn't bother you?

20:57.906 --> 20:59.657
Not at all.

21:00.287 --> 21:03.957
What you said really touched me.

21:05.414 --> 21:06.455
Take this.

21:06.455 --> 21:07.958
(Magical Physical Kululu)

21:07.958 --> 21:10.085
What? Are you sure?

21:10.085 --> 21:11.920
I want you to have it.

21:12.587 --> 21:14.214
Thank you so much!

21:14.214 --> 21:17.634
Miyako-chan's first aid
was a complete success!

21:17.634 --> 21:21.054
I knew having a chat would work!

21:21.847 --> 21:26.726
I asked my publisher to make
a statement about the mean comments.

21:26.726 --> 21:30.230
Thank you,
but don't push yourself too hard.

21:31.106 --> 21:33.276
There's no need to worry.

21:33.276 --> 21:38.989
Miyako Fuji is wearing two hats
and is determined to see it through.

21:38.989 --> 21:40.615
She's so cool.

21:42.742 --> 21:44.244
Is this a sticker?

21:44.828 --> 21:50.709
The pretty words, act-cutes, and chads...

21:51.511 --> 21:53.137
I can't stand them.

21:56.006 --> 22:03.847
Why can birds fly through the sky?
Why are cats always asleep?

22:03.847 --> 22:07.767
How will you live today?

22:07.767 --> 22:15.525
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

22:19.738 --> 22:27.494
Why does the morning sun kiss my skin?
Why does the night leave me feeling down?

22:27.494 --> 22:35.795
If only we could split our sorrows in half
Wouldn't that be great?

22:35.795 --> 22:43.678
Laughter and worry interweave
In a corner of this vast world

22:43.678 --> 22:52.061
Come with us
To uncover the wonders of the universe

22:53.063 --> 23:00.946
What stories shall we share today?
What melodies shall we sing?

23:00.946 --> 23:04.782
Even flowers as yet unseen

23:04.782 --> 23:11.998
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

23:12.707 --> 23:19.756
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

23:25.436 --> 23:26.680
Let's ask!

23:26.680 --> 23:29.641
Welcome, lost lamb. Confess your sins.

23:29.641 --> 23:31.393
I have no regrets.

23:31.393 --> 23:32.599
